  "description": "Steel Reserve 1.3 is competition ready with a full crmo SR frame with tapered head tube and rotor tabs. Its \"Six Shooter\" dropouts are interchangeable which allows you to convert it from a single speed to a multi speed derailleur set up should you choose. A Haro OS rotor comes standard on SR 1.3's tapered head tube, all mounted to a Marzocchi DJ1 100mm fork complete with thru-axle. It features a Spoon 1 1/8\" stem and Spoon 762 40mm rise bar from Spank Industries. Haro's slim padded saddle is mounted to a TriPod post to keep things light. Stopping is consistent and reliable thanks to a new unique hybrid mechanical/hydraulic disc brake from TRP. 1.3 rolls as fast as it flies on its 26\" lightweight wheel set that combines Kenda's Small Block Eight tires (2.35\" wide on the front and 2.1\" wide on the rear) with Spank Industries Spoon alloy double wall rims.\nHaro Full Crmo Steel Reserve frame w/ tapered head tube & interchangeable dropouts\nNew Haro OS rotor for tapered 1-1/8\"-1.5\" head tube\n21.8\" TT (Short) & 22.5\" TT (Long) sizes\nMarzocchi DJ1 100mm travel fork w/ 20mm thru-axle\nHaro Crmo 8 Spline 2-pc crankset, 25t sprocket\nSpank Ind. Spoon 762, 40mm rise bar\nVelo Lock On grips\nSpank Ind. Spoon 1-1/8\" stem\nHaro slim padded saddle w/ TriPod post\nSpank Ind. Spoon alloy DW 36h rims,\nPivit alloy disc cassette w/ 12t Crmo cog\nKenda Small Block Eight 2.35\"/2.10\" tires\nNew TRP HY/RD-C mechanical / hydraulic rear disc brake",
